! `@` with `^` or `+` is S, where nothing writes the stroke as struck: the
! board's `@` sits above S, so a marker chord can take S on the top row.
@^*EFR
@^+*EFRBS
! S held as well is still S
@^S*EFR
! without a marker `@` is the modifiers' namespace, S included: ctrl-S
@S-F
! with a mark no fold reads `@` as the modifiers' namespace, and ^+STP has no base
@^+TP
! the folds of the stroke with S in `@`'s place apply: sun and -y
!buffer
@^+SUPB
@^+UPB
